UID:10002756-1778697000-1778698800@www.transitionslifecare.org
SUMMARY:Maybe it’s Your Medications? (virtual)
DESCRIPTION:RSVP to Community@transitionslifecare.org \nHere are a few topics we may consider during this presentation: \n– How medication reviews improve safety\, clarity\, and confidence.\n– Understanding harmful interactions and side effects.\n– Why deprescribing is essential for reducing fall risk and cognitive decline.\n– How pharmacists collaborate with doctors to optimize care.\n– Practical steps for safer\, simpler\, and more effective medication use.\n– Real examples of how medication changes transform quality of life.\n– Q&A \nPresenter:\nDr. DeLon Canterbury\, PharmD\, BCGP\, is the CEO of GeriatRx and a nationally recognized aging-friendly care champion and deprescribing expert.\nNamed one of the Top 50 Most Influential Pharmacists in the U.S.\, he specializes in medication optimization and deprescribing to improve outcomes for older adults through collaborative\, patient-centered care.
URL:https://www.transitionslifecare.org/event/maybe-its-your-medications-virtual/
LOCATION:Virtual
CATEGORIES:Community Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.transitionslifecare.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/D1D_1753_HC4-edited-sm.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Community Engagement":MAILTO:community@transitionslifecare.org
GEO:35.7595731;-79.0192997
END:VEVENT
